          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em reflective subcategory
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C \hookrightarrow D
          %p
            such that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon d \to d'
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            have “reflections”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T d
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi d
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T f \colon T d \to T d'
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            looks at its own reflection via a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \to T d
            and the reflection of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
            is equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi c
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T c \cong c
          %p A canonical example is the inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ab
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{Ab} \hookrightarrow \mathrm{Grp}
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+abelian+groups"} category of abelian groups
            into the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+groups"} category of groups
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelianization"} abelianization
          %p
            A useful property of reflective subcategories is that the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} creates all limits
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            admits.
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : C \hookrightarrow D
              is
              %strong reflective
              if the inclusion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi T
                    %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (T \dashv i) :  C \stackrel{\stackrel{T}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    D
                    \\,.
          %p
            The left adjoint is sometimes called the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong reflector
            = succeed "." do
              %strong reflection
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
            = succeed "," do
              %strong coreflector
            = succeed "." do
              %strong coreflection
          #NonFullReflections.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              A few sources (such as
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} MacLane 1971
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} invariant under equivalence
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/30/41/30-41.pdf"} TAC paper
              by Adámek and Rosický.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The components of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mi Id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi T
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↪
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\eta}&amp; \searrow^{Id}
                    \\\
                    D &amp;\stackrel{T}{\to}&amp; C &amp;\stackrel{i}{\hookrightarrow} &amp; D
                    }
            %p
              of this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              “reflect” each object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              into its image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T d
              in the reflective subcategory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi d
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta_d : d \to T  d
                    \\,.
          %p
            This reflection is sometimes called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            (due to
            %a{:href => "reflective+localization#ReflectiveSubcategoriesAreLocalizations"} this Prop.
            at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} left exact
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              If the reflector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion"} completion
          %h2#characterizations Characterizations
          #CharacterizationByLocalization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (equivalent characterizations)
            %p
              Given any pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi L
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv R)
                    \\;:\;
                    B
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    A
            %p the following are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  is equivalent to its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  under
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                  of
                  = succeed ".)" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ε
                        %mo :
                        %mi L
                        %mi R
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon : L R \to 1_B
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                  of functors.
              %li
                %p
                  There exists some natural isomorphism
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mi R
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L R \to 1_B
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mi L
                        %mo ,
                        %mi R
                        %mi ε
                        %mi L
                        %mo ,
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R L, R\varepsilon L,\eta)
                  associated with the adjunction is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective on objects
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  is the set of morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(s)
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon A \to B
                  realizes
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  as the (nonstrict)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  with respect to the class
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+functor"} dense
          %p
            The equivalence of statements (1), (2), (4) and (5) are originally due to (
            %a{:href => "#GabrielZisman67"}> Gabriel-Zisman 67, Prop. 1.3, page 7
            ). The equivalence of (1) and (6) is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Ulmer68"}> Ulmer, Theorem 1.13
            ). The equivalence of (2) and (3) is (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, Lemma A1.1.1
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The equivalence of (1) and (2) is
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#FullyFaithfulAndInvertibleAdjoints"} this proposition
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "idempotent+monad#EquivalentConditions"} this Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi lan
                        %mi L
                      %mi L
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mi lan
                        %mi L
                      %mi id
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi L
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lan_L L \cong L lan_L id \cong L R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lan
                      %mi L
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lan_L id
              is absolute, and is isomorphic to the identity if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is fully faithful.
            %p
              To prove that (3) implies (2), the argument is to transfer the comonad structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L R
              across the isomorphism to a comonad structure on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_B
              the counit is inverse to the comultiplication; thus the counit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ε
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon
              of the original comonad structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L R
              must have been invertible. The same argument shows that for a comonad in any 2-category the counit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ε
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon : L R \to 1_B
              is an isomorphism iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L R
              is isomorphic to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_B
          %p
            This is a well-known set of equivalences concerning
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monads"} idempotent monads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon B \to A
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
            (Prop.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReflectiveSubcategoryInclusionIsMonadic"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            as the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras for the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i r
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r: A \to B
            is the reflector.
          %p
            See also the related discussion at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(infinity,1)-category
          %h2#special_cases Special cases
          %h3#ExactReflectiveSubcategories Exact reflective subcategories
          %p
            If the reflector (which as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            always preserves all
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            = succeed "." do
              %em exact
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
          %p
            In particular, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            is an exact reflective subcategory of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi sheafify
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh(C) \stackrel{\overset{sheafify}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  PSh(C)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The reflector in that case is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
            functor.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a reflective subcategory of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+ideal"} exponential ideal
              if and only if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflector"} reflector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\to C
              preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            %p
              In particular,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is then also cartesian closed.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, A4.3.1
            ). See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subuniverse"} reflective subuniverse
          %p
            So in particular if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an exact reflective subcategory of a cartesian closed category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+ideal"} exponential ideal
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day%27s+reflection+theorem"} Day's reflection theorem
            for a more general statement and proof.
          %h3#complete_reflective_subcategories Complete reflective subcategories
          %p
            When the unit of the reflector is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %em complete
            objects in some sense; the reflector takes each object in the ambient category to its completion. Such reflective subcategories are sometimes called
            = succeed "." do
              %em mono-reflective
            %em epi-reflective
            (when the unit is an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            %em bi-reflective
            (when the unit is both a monomorphism and an epimorphism).
          %p
            In the last case, note that if the unit is an
            = succeed "morphism," do
              %em iso
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/balanced+categories"} balanced categories
            %em not
            mean reflective and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+categories"} concrete categories
            (such as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+categories"} topological categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                reflective over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %h3#AccessibleReflectiveSubcategories Accessible reflective subcategories
          #AccessibleReflection.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p A reflection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    \\mathcal{D}
            %p
              is called
              %strong accessible
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
              and the reflector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\circ L \colon \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{D}
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible functor
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A reflective subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{D}
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
              is accessible, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AccessibleReflection"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
          %p
            In this explicit form this appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, prop. 5.5.1.2
            ). From (
            %a{:href => "#AdamekRosicky"}> Adamek-Rosický
            ) the “only if”-direction follows immediately from 2.53 there (saying that an accessibly embedded subcategory of an accessible category is accessible iff it is cone-reflective), while the “if”-direction follows immediately from 2.23 (saying any left or right adjoint between accessible categories is accessible).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %p
            A reflective subcategory is always closed under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limits
            which exist in the ambient category (because the full inclusion is monadic, by Prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReflectiveSubcategoryInclusionIsMonadic"}
            %a{:href => "monadic+functor#MonadicFunctorsCreateLimits"} hence
            creates limits, as noted above), and inherits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
            from the larger category by application of the reflector
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Riehl"} Riehl, Prop 4.5.15
          %p A morphism in a reflective subcategory is monic iff it is monic in the ambient category. A reflective subcategory of a well-powered category is well-powered.
          %h3#AsEilenbergMooreCategory As Eilenberg-Moore category of the idempotent monad
          %p
          #ReflectiveSubcategoryInclusionIsMonadic.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Every reflective subcategory inclusion is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} modules
              for its
              %a{:href => "monad#RelationBetweenAdjunctionsAndMonads"} induced
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
              is a reflective subcategory
          A proof is spelled out for instance in
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#Borceux94b"} Borceux 1994, vol 2, cor. 4.2.4
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+proof"} formal proof
          in
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+Agda"} cubical Agda
          is given in
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#1Lab"} 1Lab
          %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CharacterizationByLocalization"}
          and see at
          = succeed "." do
            %em
              %a{:href => "idempotent+monad#AlgebrasForAnIdempotentMonad"} idempotent monad – Properties – Algebras for an idempotent monad and localization
          %h3#reflective_subcategories_of_locally_presentable_categories Reflective subcategories of locally presentable categories
          %p
            Both the weak and strong versions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vop%C4%9Bnka%27s+principle"} Vopěnka's principle
            are equivalent to fairly simple statements concerning reflective subcategories of locally presentable categories:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              The weak
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vop%C4%9Bnka%27s+principle"} Vopěnka's principle
              is equivalent to the statement:
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \hookrightarrow C
              which is closed under
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
          %p
            This is
            %a{:href => "#AdamekRosicky"} AdamekRosicky, theorem 6.28
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              The strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vop%C4%9Bnka%27s+principle"} Vopěnka's principle
              is equivalent to:
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \hookrightarrow C
              which is closed under
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is then also locally presentable.
          %p
            (Remark after corollary 6.24 in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AdamekRosicky"} Adamek-Rosicky book
          %h3#ReflectiveSubcategoriesOfCartesianClosedCategotries Reflective subcategories of cartesian closed categories
          %p
            In showing that a given category is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is cartesian closed, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\subseteq C
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\colon C\to D
              preserves finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+ideal"} exponential ideal
              (i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\in D
              implies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X\in D
              for any
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves finite products, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is cartesian closed.
          %h3#reflective_and_coreflective_subcategories Reflective and coreflective subcategories
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_5 Theorem
            %p
              A subcategory of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A^{op}, Set]
              which is both reflective and coreflective is itself a category of presheaves
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B^{op}, Set]
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
          %p
            This is shown in (
            %a{:href => "#BashirVelebil"}> BashirVelebil
            ).
          %h3#property_vs_structure Property vs structure
          %p
            Whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a full subcategory of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            with some extra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property%2C+structure%2C+stuff"} property
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is reflective in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            as objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with (if we're lucky) some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            or (in any case) some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+stuff"} extra stuff
          %p
            This can always be made to work by brute force, but sometimes there is something insightful about it. For example, a metric space is a complete metric space equipped with a dense subset. Or, an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            equipped with numerator and denominator functions.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Complete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
              are mono-reflective in metric spaces; the reflector is called
              = succeed "." do
                %em completion
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a reflective subcategory of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              on
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AccessibleReflection"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+inclusion"} geometric inclusion
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              A category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+presheaves"} concrete presheaves
              inside a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+site"} concrete site
              is a reflective subcategory.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recollement"} recollement
              situation, we have several reflectors and coreflectors. We have a reflective and coreflective subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_*: A' \hookrightarrow A
              with reflector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*
              and coreflector
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^!
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^*
              is both a reflector for the reflective subcategory
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ″
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_*: A'' \hookrightarrow A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mo !
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ″
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_!: A'' \hookrightarrow A
          #TheReflectiveSubcategoriesOfSet.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              Assuming classical logic, the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              has exactly three reflective (and
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/replete+subcategory"} replete
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton sets
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingletons"} subsingletons
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              itself.
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
              = succeed "-sheaves" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          #AffineVarieties.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
              is a reflective subcategory of the category of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto Spec \Gamma(X,\mathcal{O}_X)
            %p
              The generalization of this example to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              is discussed at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras+on+infinity-stacks"} function algebras on infinity-stacks
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
              is in (
              %a{:href => "#Rosenberg98"}> Rosenberg 98, prop 4.4.3
              ).
          #NonUnitalRings.num_example
            %h6#counterexample (Counter)Example
            %p
              The non-full inclusion of unital
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
              into non-unital rings has a left adjoint (with monic units), whose reflector formally adjoins an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+element"} identity element
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonFullReflections"}
          #RemarkOnNonUnitalRings.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Notice that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ring
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in Ring
              a ring with unit, its reflection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L R
              in the above example is not in general isomorphic to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "\u2018" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ring
                      %mo ↪
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ring
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Ring} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{Ring}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              (as any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              between varieties of algebras, by the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+lifting+theorem"} adjoint lifting theorem
              = succeed "\u2019" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ring
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Ring}
          #CategoryOfCategories.num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p The subcategory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat \hookrightarrow sSet
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+categories"} category of categories
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} category of simplical sets
              is a reflective subcategory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Riehl"} Riehl, example 4.5.14 (vi)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              is complete and cocomplete because it inherits all limits and colimits from
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
          #ModelsOfALawvereTheory.num_example
            %h6#example_8 Example
            %p
              For any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Prod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prod(T, Set)
            %p
              of product preserving functors into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              and natural transformations between them. The inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Prod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prod(T, Set) \hookrightarrow [T, Set]
            %p
              is a reflective subcategory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Buckley"} Buckley, theorem 5.2.1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [T,Set]
              is complete and cocomplete (limits and colimits are computed pointwise), so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Prod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prod(T, Set)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mon"} Mon
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"}> localization
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+reflection"}> Quillen reflection
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localization"} left Bousfield localization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(infinity,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bireflective+subcategory"} bireflective subcategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+cylinder"}> adjoint cylinder
                , describing the situation when the reflector has a further left adjoint
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes+are+equivalently+the+left+exact+reflective+subcategories+of+presheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes are equivalently the left exact reflective subcategories of presheaf toposes
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#GabrielZisman67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"}> Pierre Gabriel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michel+Zisman"} Michel Zisman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calculus+of+fractions+and+homotopy+theory"} Calculus of fractions and homotopy theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.math.rochester.edu/faculty/doug/otherpapers/GZ.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Ulmer68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Friedrich+Ulmer"}> Friedrich Ulmer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Properties of Dense and Relative Adjoint Functors
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , §IV.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                %strong 5
                Springer (1971, second ed. 1997) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Borceux94a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , p. 196 in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Basic Category Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525858"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525858
            %li#Borceux94b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Cor. 4.2.4 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories and Structures
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525865"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525865
            %li#AdamekRosicky
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jiri+Adamek"}> Jiri Adamek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locally+presentable+and+accessible+categories"} Locally presentable and accessible categories
                London Mathematical Society Lecture Note Series 189
            %li
              %p
                Springer eom:
                %a{:href => "http://eom.springer.de/r/r080550.htm"} reflective subcategory
            %li
              %p
                C. Cassidy, M. Hébert,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+M.+Kelly"} G. M. Kelly
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Reflective subcategories, localizations and factorizationa systems
                = succeed ":3" do
                  %strong 38
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S1446788700023624"} doi
            %li
              %p
                cf. the notion of
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Q
                          %mo ∘
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q^\circ
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Q-category"} Q-category
            %li#Riehl
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                , p. 142 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Category+Theory+in+Context"} Category Theory in Context
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://emilyriehl.github.io/files/context.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Buckley
              %p
                Mitchell Buckley,
                %em
                  Lawvere Theories, 2008
                  %a{:href => "http://web.science.mq.edu.au/~street/MitchB.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The relation of exponential ideals to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategories"} reflective subcategories
            is discussed in section A4.3.1 of
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
          %p Reflective and coreflective subcategories of presheaf categories are discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BashirVelebil
              R. Bashir, J. Velebil,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Simultaneously reflective and coreflective subcategories of presheaves
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/TAC/volumes/10/16/10-16.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Related discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-categories
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p
            The example of affine schemes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Rosenberg98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"}> Alexander Rosenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutative schemes
          %p
            Formalization in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+Agda"} cubical Agda
          %ul
            %li#1Lab
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1lab"}> 1lab
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://1lab.dev/Cat.Functor.Adjoint.Reflective.html"} Reflective Subcategories
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Kennison"} John Kennison
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Raphael"} Robert Raphael
